WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.680
DC Comics fans are up in arms&nbsp;
over a helmet in "Black Adam."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.880
Here's why they just can't get over&nbsp;
what they call a major oversight.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.360
Whether you hate "Black Adam,"&nbsp;
like the critics do, or love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.800
Dwayne Johnson's biggest box office opening&nbsp;
as a leading man as the audience seems to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.520
it offers some hints about the&nbsp;
DC Extended Universe's future.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.880
There's a lot of speculation about&nbsp;
developments in the movie and how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.380
these elements might play in future&nbsp;
DCEU outings, like another movie with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.100
Henry Cavill's Superman, as revealed in&nbsp;
the mid-credits scene of "Black Adam."

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:37.080
If you saw the movie, you know that Dr.&nbsp;
Fate died saving Hawkman from Sabbac,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:43.537
leaving the fate of the Helmet of Fate at play.&nbsp;
The helmet goes to Hawkman, who uses its powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.537 --> 00:00:48.960
magic. Hawkman keeps Sabbac occupied long enough&nbsp;
for Black Adam to show up and save the day.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:54.120
In doing so, he creates a decoy version of&nbsp;
himself and appears to fall when attacked by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.380
the supervillain, showing fans how Dr.&nbsp;
Fate's vision has played out. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.280
it turns out that fans are a bit&nbsp;
confused by this development. Here's why.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.920
"Let me show you, my friend!"

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:12.480
Throughout "Black Adam," fans learn a few things&nbsp;
about the Helmet of Fate that gives Dr. Fate his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.820
abilities and powers. One: it's "alien."&nbsp;
Two: only the worthy can even touch it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.000
as noted in a conversation aboard&nbsp;
the Justice Society's airship.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.700
Lastly, putting it on exacts a toll on the&nbsp;
wearer, which gets exhausting. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:32.160
what happens when the helmet "turns on" is that&nbsp;
the wearer is "possessed," as Dr. Fate explains.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:37.860
This helmet has a long history in DC Comics lore.&nbsp;
Although the movie seems to be taking from that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:41.880
lore, it's not staying completely accurate.&nbsp;
In the comics, the helmet is not an alien&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.800
object but an ancient one created by the Lords of&nbsp;
Order, who were present at the dawn of humanity.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:52.620
It is truly a coveted object, turning its wearer&nbsp;
into one of the most powerful superheroes in DC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:57.660
canon. And, as pointed out in the film, it has&nbsp;
some choice regarding who can wear it and when.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:01.020
In the movie, the helmet's powers&nbsp;
include the ability to see into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:06.420
future and to project multiple images of&nbsp;
oneself, telekinesis, and invulnerability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:10.620
which are just a tiny fraction of the powers&nbsp;
the helmet bestows wearers in the comics.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:16.080
Those abilities, in different DC properties,&nbsp;
have also included manipulating natural elements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:21.420
like fire, air, water, and earth. In DC canon,&nbsp;
the helmet comes along with two other items:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.400
the Amulet of Anubis and the Cloak of&nbsp;
Destiny, which also grant additional powers.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.200
Given the long history of the helmet, fans&nbsp;
are definitely going to have opinions about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.760
it. And in the case of "Black Adam," fans&nbsp;
are upset and perhaps a bit unsure about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.240
a few things. The thing is, the&nbsp;
helmet doesn't necessarily just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.260
turn on when the user wants it to —&nbsp;
at least, not when first taken up.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:49.560
Nabu, the god in charge of the helmet, is still&nbsp;
a soul present within it. He must deem each user&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:55.260
worthy before granting the powers that come with&nbsp;
the helmet. This requires a period of judgment.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:00.720
In fact, numerous people who wore the helmet have&nbsp;
found it difficult to bear the mental load. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:06.240
DC's New 52 world, Khalid Ben-Hassin suffered&nbsp;
bouts of insanity after donning it, but others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:10.200
who couldn't handle the helmet were criminals&nbsp;
who stole it from their rightful wearers.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.580
This means, of course, that the scene in which&nbsp;
Hawkman is deemed good enough to exact the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:19.920
helmet's vengeance on Sabbac shouldn't actually&nbsp;
have happened as it did. On fan posted on Twitter,

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.267
"I just wanted to scream&nbsp;
'THAT'S NOT HOW THAT WORKS!'"

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:27.060
Another fan expressed confusion&nbsp;
about Hawkman not getting fatigued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.440
after using the helmet and its magic.&nbsp;
Another was also confused and believed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.040
the Helmet of Fate to be far too&nbsp;
powerful for just anyone to wear.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.340
As with all DC history, though, canon has evolved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:43.260
and different interpretations of the character&nbsp;
have popped up in various projects, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:49.511
"Smallville" and a brief appearance in "Legends&nbsp;
of Tomorrow." The DCEU is changing things again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.511 --> 00:03:53.845
which may inform the direction the&nbsp;
cinematic universe takes in the future.

